port this code to python:
```perl
sub find_longest_substring_with_repeated_characters {
    my ($text) = @_;
    my @freq = (0) x 26;
    my $left = 0;
    my $right = 0;
    my $max_len = 0;

    while ($right < length($text)) {
        $freq[ord(substr($text, $right, 1)) - ord('a')]++;
        my $max_freq = (sort {$b <=> $a} @freq)[0];
        while ($right - $left + 1 - $max_freq > 1) {
            $freq[ord(substr($text, $left, 1)) - ord('a')]--;
            $left++;
            $max_freq = (sort {$b <=> $a} @freq)[0];
        }
        $max_len = $right - $left + 1 if ($right - $left + 1 > $max_len);
        $right++;
    }

    return $max_len;
}
```

You are tasked with implementing a vote counting system for a local election. The system should be able to process and print the results of the votes cast by the constituents. The vote counting system is represented by the following Python code snippet:

```python
class VoteCounter:
    def __init__(self):
        self.results = {}

    def cast_vote(self, candidate):
        if candidate in self.results:
            self.results[candidate] += 1
        else:
            self.results[candidate] = 1

    def print_vote_results(self):
        for candidate, votes in self.results.items():
            print(f"{candidate}: {votes} votes")

# Example usage
vote = VoteCounter()
vote.cast_vote("Candidate A")
vote.cast_vote("Candidate B")
vote.cast_vote("Candidate A")
vote.print_vote_results()
```

Your task is to complete the implementation of the `VoteCounter` class by filling in the missing parts of the code. The `cast_vote` method should take a candidate's name as input and increment the vote count for that candidate. If the candidate has not received any votes yet, their name should be added to the results with an initial count of 1. The `print_vote_results` method should iterate through the results and print the name of each candidate along with the total number of votes they received.

Write a Python class `VoteCounter` that fulfills the requirements outlined above.

port this code to python:
```dart
class TreeNode {
  int val;
  TreeNode left;
  TreeNode right;

  TreeNode(this.val, [this.left = null, this.right = null]);
}

int findSecondMinimumValue(TreeNode root, [int current = -1]) {
  if (root == null) {
    return current;
  }
  if (current == -1 || root.val < current) {
    current = root.val;
  }
  if (root.left != null && root.right != null) {
    if (root.val == root.left.val) {
      current = findSecondMinimumValue(root.left, current);
      if (root.val != root.right.val) {
        current = current == -1 ? root.right.val : current < root.right.val ? current : root.right.val;
      }
    } else {
      current = findSecondMinimumValue(root.right, current);
      if (root.val != root.left.val) {
        current = current == -1 ? root.left.val : current < root.left.val ? current : root.left.val;
      }
    }
  }
  return current;
}
```

